{"section_id":"","widget_updates":[{"widget_id":"6fe9fbe","widget_type":"text-editor","settings":{"editor":"<p>Use this form for routine questions and <a href="https://erofwhiterock.com/insurance-billing-info/">billing inquiries</a>. It is not monitored for emergencies. If you think you have a medical emergency, call 911 and do not wait for a form response.</p>","custom_css":"
selector a, selector a:hover, selector a:focus { color: #FFFFFF !important; text-decoration: underline; }
selector a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #FFFFFF; outline-offset: 3px; }"}},{"widget_id":"8a94fb1","widget_type":"text-editor","settings":{"editor":"<p>Laboratory tests help the medical team assess your symptoms and decide the next steps in your care.</p>"}},{"widget_id":"75441c43","widget_type":"text-editor","settings":{"editor":"<p>ER of White Rock provides laboratory testing as part of emergency care. Ask what each result means and whether follow-up is needed.</p>"}},{"widget_id":"260980fe","widget_type":"text-editor","settings":{"editor":"<p>Blood and urine tests provide information to help evaluate an illness or injury. Your clinician decides which tests are needed.</p><ul><li><strong>Complete blood count:</strong> Measures blood cells and can offer clues about anemia or infection.</li><li><strong>Metabolic panel:</strong> Helps assess glucose, electrolytes and organ function.</li><li><strong>Cardiac and coagulation tests:</strong> Are interpreted alongside symptoms, examination and other tests. One result does not rule out every emergency.</li><li><strong>Urinalysis:</strong> May help evaluate urinary symptoms. Treatment depends on the findings and medical assessment.</li></ul>"}},{"widget_id":"231ddd11","widget_type":"text-editor","settings":{"editor":"<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-75917348 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent e-lazyloaded" data-id="75917348" data-element_type="container" data-settings="{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}"><div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2529a93b elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="2529a93b" data-element_type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default"><div class="elementor-widget-container"><p>When you are facing a medical crisis or need fast diagnostic answers, waiting days for an outside lab is not an option. At <a href="https://erofwhiterock.com/"><strong>ER of White Rock</strong></a>, our 24/7 freestanding ER features a fully equipped, COLA-certified on-site laboratory. Whether you require life-saving cardiac panels, complex blood cultures, or rapid viral testing, our experienced emergency physicians rely on our in-house technology to deliver results that support clinical evaluation. Experience highly capable diagnostic medicine with minimal wait times right here in East Dallas.</p><p>On-site lab testing is the core differentiator between emergency care and urgent care. Our <a href="https://erofwhiterock.com/freestanding-er-vs-hospital-er-near-white-rock-lake/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">guide to emergency care near White Rock</a> explains how diagnostics differ between the two settings.</p></div></div></div>"}},{"widget_id":"407ce12a","widget_type":"text-editor","settings":{"editor":"<p>Medical emergencies do not operate on a schedule, and neither do we. We have streamlined our laboratory process to get you evaluated and tested immediately.</p><ul><li><strong>Step 1: Walk-In 24/7</strong> Do not wait for an appointment. Drive directly to our modern facility anytime, day or night, and experience our standard of minimal wait times.</li><li><strong>Step 2: Rapid Physician Triage</strong> If you are experiencing pain or severe symptoms, our experienced emergency doctors will evaluate you instantly to determine exactly which lab tests are required to save your life.</li><li><strong>Step 3: On-Site Sample Collection</strong> Our skilled, compassionate registered nurses will draw your blood or collect necessary swabs quickly and safely in a private room.</li><li><strong>Step 4: Fast, Accurate Results</strong> Your samples are walked directly to our in-house lab. Timing varies by test. Before leaving, ask which results are still pending and how follow-up will be arranged.</li></ul>"}},{"widget_id":"7f81724","widget_type":"flip-box","settings":{"description_text_b":"COVID-19 tests help assess possible infection. Your clinician interprets results in light of symptoms and test timing."}},{"widget_id":"5a5be3b"