}</script>"}},{"widget_id":"4b311a94","widget_type":"text-editor","settings":{"editor":"<p>While our East Dallas facility is here to provide life-saving care, understanding stroke prevention is just as important for protecting your family. The <a href="https://www.ninds.nih.gov/health-information/disorders/stroke">NIH NINDS</a> identifies high blood pressure as the leading cause of strokes and brain bleeds. If you or a loved one have a history of hypertension, taking proactive steps is vital:</p><ul><li><strong>Manage Blood Pressure:</strong> Check your levels regularly and take all prescribed medications.</li><li><strong>Control Diabetes:</strong> High blood sugar damages blood vessels over time and increases clot risks.</li><li><strong>Quit Smoking:</strong> Smoking thickens your blood and drastically increases the chance of plaque buildup.</li><li><strong>Watch for Warning Signs:</strong> Sudden dizziness, severe unexplained headaches, or temporary vision loss are warning signs that require calling 911 immediately.</li></ul>"}},{"widget_id":"898932f","widget_type":"text-editor","settings":{"editor":"<p>Use this form for routine questions and <a href="https://erofwhiterock.com/insurance-billing-info/">billing inquiries</a>. It is not monitored for emergencies. If you think you have a medical emergency, call 911 and do not wait for a form response.</p>"}}]}
